fujinet-go-studio2-desktop -- milestone log
===========================================

The plan is the family's (see fujinet-go-adam-desktop/PORTING.md): one C API
in core/, four native frontends, FujiNet in-process, one shared settings
store, a native debugger everywhere, no panels visible at startup,
clone-and-build CI. The core is MAME's RCA Studio II transposed to C, the
astrocade and SMS siblings' way; the session, debugger and frontends are the
SMS sibling's. Plan: ~/.claude/plans/build-fujinet-go-desktop-swirling-rabbit.md.
Nothing below is marked done on "it compiles".

M0  scaffold                                                          [x]
  [x] root CMakeLists (VERSION 0.1.0, FRONTEND switch, WITH_STUDIO2_ROMS OFF,
      no_embedded_roms registration, icon loop, CPack DEB/RPM/TGZ)
  [x] cmake/Dependencies.cmake pins fujinet-firmware master (8fa1727b2, #2083);
      cmake/StageFujiProto.cmake stages pico/studio2 + pico/common
  [x] tools/fujinet: BoIP 11518, web UI 11519; patch 0001 (default hosts);
      the post-#1960 transforms (-Werror off when embedded, pyyaml/jinja2
      pip fallback); every heredoc anchor audited against the pin

M1  CPU                                                               [x]
  [x] cpu1802.c: MAME's cosmac.cpp state machine, CDP1802 subset
  [x] dasm1802.c: MAME's cosdasm; dasm test against MAME's own output for
      all 256 opcodes (dasm_golden.h, from MAME's debugger)

M2  machine                                                           [x]
  [x] cdp1861.c: MAME's three timers as absolute clocks, time_until_pos
      transposed, flat 112-pixel bitmap rows
  [x] machine.c: memory/I-O maps, keypads on EF3/EF4 via the OUT 2 latch,
      INP 1, Q -> 300 Hz beeper, CLEAR (resets the 1861 on the press)
  [x] tools/ab/mame_ab.py: BIOS alone with keys, 8 carts (DIRECT, against
      MAME's FujiNet device), CONFIG: every frame pixel-identical; Lua keys
      land two frames late in MAME (--key-shift -2)
  [x] power-on pulses CLEAR (IE=1) unlike MAME (IE=0); --mame-power-on for A/B,
      with Clear pressed first (MAME's BIOS never takes its interrupt
      otherwise): 1200/1200 frames, 8 carts + the built-ins
  [x] beeper: mame_ab.py --wav, every beep within two samples of MAME's

M3  cartridge                                                         [x]
  [x] fujinet_cart.c from studio2_fujinet.cpp; worker thread, poke queue,
      FN_R_LINK, reconnecting wait_link_ms, busy status
  [x] fujitcp_host.c (the SMS twin; master's fujitcp.c now has abort too)
  [x] stub.asm/stub.c: the no-BIOS stand-in; parks on a game, the machine
      blanks the picture and the session asks for the BIOS
  [x] tests: stub_boot, cart (loopback FujiNet: push, stage, arm, swap, the
      trace tap byte-for-byte), cart_seam (pages, peeks, the qualified
      read of $0000, CLEAR into an armed CONFIG), mame_trace, no_sdl_link

M4  session                                                           [x]
  [x] studio2session.h: keypads + CLEAR targets, Import BIOS (2K / 1K / the
      four ROMs), use_bios, games refused with no BIOS, needs_bios
  [x] tests: session, bindings, media, gamepad, gamepad_map, boot_smoke,
      fujibus_smoke, config_boot (an app and a game booted from the SD
      host), netboot + netboot_sync (fujitest, fujiboot)

M5  debugger engine                                                   [x]
  [x] studio2debug.h: 1802 registers, SEP/SCRT step over/out, CDP1861 state
      and views, I/O, cart page map and text engine, AS symbol formats,
      big-endian {addr}
  [x] tests: debug, fujitrace

M6  GNOME                                                             [ ]
M7  KDE                                                               [x]
  [x] Qt6 port of the SMS frontend: menus, needs-BIOS alert, Keypad window
      (fixed-size floating), Preferences' BIOS line, the debugger's 8 tabs
  [x] seen under Hyprland on a headless output: CONFIG with a live FujiNet,
      keypad held keys, Preferences before/after Import BIOS, every
      debugger tab, the needs-BIOS alert, a game after import
  [ ] not seen: Map mode, menu accelerators, About (no click dispatcher;
      Hyprland's synthetic keys lose Ctrl for Qt)
M8  Windows                                                           [ ]
M9  macOS (CI only: no Apple toolchain here)                          [~]
  [x] AppKit port of the SMS frontend; every API name and arity checked
      against the headers by script
  [ ] first build is CI's

M10 packaging + CI                                                    [~]
  [x] icons: the family mark, inverted, on #C8B58C
  [x] flatpak manifests pinned to master (type: git); NSIS installer
  [ ] screenshots (CONFIG, the debugger, the keypad)
  [ ] CI green on every workflow

M11 family audit                                                      [~]
  core and tools against the SMS sibling (names normalised):
  [x] cart_seam ported (Studio II seam: pages, peeks, hand-over, CLEAR)
  [x] sms_drive -> studio2_drive (whole app headless, scripted)
  [x] audio_ab.py -> mame_ab.py --wav (one harness for frames and audio)
  not adopted, deliberately:
  - bios_synth: the Sega BIOS socket/paging/snoop; the Studio II has no
    BIOS paging, and stub_boot runs a BIOS of the tests' own
  - vdp_decode, vdp_timing, probe_golden + tools/ab/probes, make_goldens:
    covered by mame_trace (every CPU and DMA read of the tests' own BIOS,
    game and CONFIG, cycle-stamped, against MAME's trace) and dasm
  - abshot.lua: abdump.lua dumps every frame instead of snapshots
  - patch 0002 (.SMS as ROM media): master already maps .ST2
  - the firmware's fujitest/fujiboot.trace replays: pico/studio2's own
    host_test/test_cycles replays them against the same staged sources
  [ ] frontends against SMS's, once GNOME and Windows land
M12 publish (repo, v0.1.0)                                            [ ]

Not yet done / known differences
  - macOS: written to the family's AppKit pattern, CI-verified only.
  - No hardware exists for the cartridge (the firmware README's open
    questions); everything here is held to MAME.
